ombines with two water molecules to form the tetrahydroxyborate anion [B(OH)_{4}]^{−}. ... Electrolysis of a concentrated aqueous solution of 20% NaBO_{2}·4H_{2}O with an anion exchange membrane and inert anode (such as gold, palladium, or boron-doped diamond) converts the metaborate anion to tetraborate B_{4}O2−7, and the sodium salt of the later (borax) precipitates as a white powder.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n四硼酸鈉 (https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%9B%9B%E7%A1%BC%E9%85%B8%E9%88%89)\nciteturn50search20 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Sodium tetraborate \n\ndecahydrate ...  CAS号  | 1303-96-4（十水合物） ^{  check } ... * 1/B4O7.2Na.10H2O/c5-1-7-3-9-2(6)10-4(8-1)11-3;;;;;;;;;;;;/h;;;10*1H2/q-2;2*+1;;;;;;;;;;\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSodium pentaborate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_pentaborate)\nciteturn50search21 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.3 years ago; * 131634859 ... Sodium pentaborate, more properly disodium decaborate, is a chemical compound of sodium, boron, and oxygen; a salt with elemental formula NaB_{5}O_{8}, Na_{2}B_{10}O_{16}, or Na_{2}O·5B_{2}O_{3}. ... Sodium pentaborate \"dihydrate\" has the elemental formula NaH_{4}B_{5}O_{10}, which can be parsed as NaB_{5}O_{8}·2H_{2}O or Na_{2}O·5B_{3}O_{3}·4H_{2}O, however the correct formula seems to be either Na^{+}[B_{5}O_{6}(OH)_{4}]^{−} or Na^{+}[B_{5}O_{7}(OH)_{2}]^{−}·H_{2}O.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSolubility table (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solubility_table)\nciteturn50search22 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago;  Sodium tetraborate (decahydrate) | Na_{2}B_{4}O_{7}·10H_{2}O | 2 | 2.3 | 2.5 | 4 | 6 | 10 | 15 |  |  |  | 65.5\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTetraborate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetraborate)\nciteturn50search23 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.8 years ago; The hydrated tetraborate anion occurs in the mineral borax (sodium tetraborate octahydrate) with the formula Na_{2}[B_{4}O_{5}(OH)_{4}]·8H_{2}O.\n",
