01: suitable for SM 4500 - NH3\nL202: ### vapor pressure\nL203: \nL204: 0.213 hPa ( 20 °C)\nL205: \nL206: ### assay\nL207: \nL208: ≥99.5%\nL209: \nL210: ### form\nL211: \nL212: powder or crystals\nL213: \nL214: ### impurities\nL215: \nL216: ≤0.005% Insoluble matter\nL217: \nL218: ### pH\nL219: \nL220: 9.15-9.20 (25 °C, 0.01 M in solution)\nL221: \nL222: ### density\nL223: \nL224: 1.73 g/mL at 25 °C (lit.)\nL225: \nL226: ### anion traces\nL227: \nL228: chloride (Cl^{-}): ≤0.001%, phosphate (PO_{4}^{3-}): ≤0.001%, sulfate (SO_{4}^{2-}): ≤0.005%\nL229: \nL230: ### cation traces\nL231: \nL232: Ca: ≤0.005%, Fe: ≤5 ppm, heavy metals (as Pb): ≤0.001%\nL233: \nL234: ### SMILES string\nL235: \nL236: O.O.O.O.O.O.O.O.O.O.[Na+].[Na+].[O-]B1Ob2ob([O-])ob(O1)o2\nL237: ### InChI\nL238: \nL239: 1S/B4O7.2Na.10H2O/c5-1-7-3-9-2(6)10-4(8-1)11-3;;;;;;;;;;;;/h;;;10*1H2/q-2;2*+1;;;;;;;;;;\nL240: \nL241: ### InChI key\nL242: \nL243: CDMADVZSLOHIFP-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL244: \nL245: Description\nL246: \nL247: ### General description\nL248: \nL249: Sodium tetraborate decahydrate is a naturally occurring material used as a catalyst or additive for many organic transformations such as Nef reaction, Knoevenagel condensation, substitution, addition, selective methylation of vicinal diols, and desilylation of trimethylsilyl alkynones.\nL250: ### Application\nL251: \nL252: Sodium tetraborate decahydrate can be used as a catalyst in the:\nL253: \nL254:   * Regioselective thiolysis of 1,2-epoxides by using thiols to synthesize β-hydroxy sulfides.\nL255:   * Hetero-Michael addition of thiols with electron-deficient olefins to synthesize corresponding β-adducts.\nL256:   * Solvent-free Biginelli reaction to synthesize 3,4-dihydropyrimidin-2(1H)-ones.\nL257: It can also be used as an additive to prepare polypyrrole-borax composites with high dielectric properties.\nL258: \nL259: ### Legal Information\nL260: \nL261: * * *\nL262: ## Compare Similar Items\nL263: \nL264: 【18†View Full Comparison】\nL265: \nL266: *